      "value": "**Status: DRAFT — working document, not yet reviewed.** Purpose: reconcile every place \"our integrations\" are listed, before we cut any Jira epics or action items. Once this is settled, the output becomes epics (one per integration with real PWA-side work) with action items/open questions as sub-tasks. Please comment/edit directly — nothing here is final.\n\nWhy this page exists\n--------------------\n\nTim asked \"are these all our integrations?\" while we were scoping Jira epics from the repo's consolidated open-items list. The answer turned out to be no — there are **four sources**, each with a different count, and none of them agree:\n\n| Source | Location | Count | Organising principle |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Architecture matrix | repo `.claude/docs/architecture.md` (Third-Party Integrations table) | 28 | One row per vendor — the most complete single technical list |\n| Integration status tracker | repo `.claude/docs/memory/projectState.md` | 18 | Mock / Live / Not-started tracker — a *subset* of the 28 |\n| Consolidated open items | repo `.claude/docs/design/openItems.md` | 18 (40 items) | Only vendors with a known client-confirmation gap |\n| Integration Register (this Confluence section) | 9 child pages (Product, PDP, Checkout, Order History, Order Details, My Account, Store Details, Inventory Sync, MuleSoft Overview) | 30 unique INT-IDs (parent page claims 34) | One row per **page where a vendor is used** — the same vendor can (and does) appear on multiple pages under the same INT-ID |\n\nThe repo and Confluence were clearly built independently and have since drifted. Below is the reconciliation.\n\nMaster vendor list (union of all four sources)\n----------------------------------------------\n\nLegend: ✅ present · — not present · **NEW** = not in the repo at all\n\n| Vendor / System | architecture.md | projectState.md status | openItems.md | Confluence INT-ID(s) | Confluence status | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| SFCC | ✅ | ✅ Mock | ✅ (2 items) | — (platform itself) | — |  |\n| MuleSoft | ✅ | ✅ Mock | ✅ (4 items) | INT-033 | Under Review | ~~ID collision — INT-033 also used for Measmerize~~**Resolved 2026-07-07** — Measmerize moved to INT-034 on the PDP register page. |\n| NewStore OMS | ✅ | ✅ Not started | — **gap** | INT-014 | Under Review (Confirmed on Store Details) | architecture.md flags an explicit open item (customer-ID mechanism on read path) that never made it into openItems.md. Confluence has *four* separate open questions across PDP / Order History / Order Details / Inventory Sync — all more granular than the repo. |\n| AP21 | ✅ | ✅ Not started | — **gap** | INT-013 | Under Review | architecture.md says \"feed cadence/field set TBC\"; Confluence separately flags attribute-taxonomy ownership and OCI location-group IDs. Different aspects of the same gap — worth merging. |\n| Omneo | ✅ | ✅ Not started | ✅ (3 items, \"hard blockers\") | INT-023 | Under Review | Confluence's open item (Omneo *API* auth method, SFCC-side) is distinct from the repo's (iframe embed auth, front-end side) — both real, both needed. |\n| Emarsys | ✅ | ✅ Not started | — (no PWA item) | INT-024 | **Not Required** | Confluence confirms: no direct SFCC↔Emarsys integration, routes via Omneo. Consistent with repo. |\n| Adyen | ✅ | ✅ Not started | ✅ (2 items) | INT-005 | **Confirmed** | Confluence shows this further along than the repo's \"Not started\" status suggests — worth a status sync. |\n| Global-e | ✅ | ✅ Not started | ✅ (2 items) | INT-007 (checkout), INT-021 (post-purchase order status), INT-022 (returns portal) | Confirmed (007) / Under Review (021, 022) | Confluence splits one vendor into 3 tracked surfaces; repo treats it as one. New open questions: order-sync/reconciliation mechanism (007), returns-link source-system flag (021), how SFCC distinguishes international vs domestic orders (022) — none of these are in the repo. |\n| Booxi | ✅ | — (missing from tracker) | ✅ (4 items) | — **not in register at all** | — | Confluence register has no page/row for Booxi. |\n| Narvar | ✅ (one row) | ✅ Not started | ✅ (2 items) | INT-018 (EDD/Promise), INT-019 (CARE/tracking), INT-020 (returns) | Under Review (all 3) | Same split-vs-single pattern as Global-e. New questions: is EDD real-time API or SFCC-rule-based (018); tracking URL source (019); return-eligibility check location (020, this one *is* echoed in the repo's ENH-014 unresolved dependency). |\n| Contentful | ✅ | ✅ Mock | ✅ (3 items) | INT-002 | Under Review | Confluence's open questions (content-type mapping, PDP vs PLP structure) read as more basic/early than where the repo's actual build has gotten to (content-type sync script exists, ShoppableImage component built) — Confluence looks stale here. |\n| Vimeo | ✅ | — (missing from tracker) | ✅ (2 items) | INT-003 | Under Review |  |\n| Didomi | ✅ | ✅ Not started | ✅ (2 items) | INT-011 | **Confirmed** |  |\n| Google Maps API | ✅ | ✅ Not started | ✅ (1 item) | INT-009 (as \"Google Places API\") | **Confirmed** |  |\n| GTM | ✅ | — (missing from tracker) | ✅ (2 items) | INT-031 (as \"GA4 / GTM\") | Under Review | Appears on almost every register page — highest-frequency INT-ID. |\n| Optimizely Web | ✅ | — (missing from tracker) | ✅ (1 item) | — **not in register at all** | — |  |\n| Crazy Egg | ✅ | — (missing from tracker) | ✅ (3 items) | — **not in register at all** | — |  |\n| Avalara | ✅ | ✅ Not started | — (no PWA item; looked resolved) | INT-008 | Under Review | Repo reads as settled (cartridge, EU domestic confirmed); Confluence still has the integration *method* itself open (direct SFCC↔Avalara vs via MuleSoft). Real conflict, not just a gap. |\n| GiveX | ✅ | ✅ Not started | ✅ (3 items) | INT-012 (as \"Give-X\") | Under Review | Consistent with repo (NewStore adaptor for redemption/balance). |\n| Transperfect | ✅ | ✅ Not started | — **gap** | — **not in register at all** | — | architecture.md flags \"translation workflow trigger TBD\"